1
00:00:02,254 --> 00:00:10,628
Google 刚刚从 Anthropic 和 OpenAI 手中夺回了 AI 领域的榜首，
而且地球上几乎没人被允许使用这个模型。
Google just took the number one spot in AI back from Anthropic and OpenAI,
and almost nobody on the planet is allowed to use the model that did it.

2
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:12,708
它叫 Gemini 4 Carbon。
It's called Gemini 4 Carbon.

3
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:22,212
自从它第一次泄露以来，我们就一直在关注它，直到 10 月 28 日，Google 终于正式发布了它，
就在 Alphabet 季度财报电话会议前大约三小时。
We've been following it since it first leaked, and on October 28th, Google finally made it official,
about three hours before Alphabet's quarterly earnings call.

4
00:00:22,606 --> 00:00:33,860
几小时内，它就登上了 Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index 的榜首，
这是该行业最接近中立计分板的东西，它领先于 Claude Opus 5.5 和 GPT-6 Astra。
Within hours, it was sitting at the top of the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index,
the closest thing this industry has to a neutral scoreboard, ahead of Claude Opus 5.5 and ahead of GPT-6 Astra.

5
00:00:34,286 --> 00:00:38,000
影响力人士开始称其为今年最伟大的「杰迪反击」。
Influencers started calling it the greatest Jedi counterattack of the year.

6
00:00:38,286 --> 00:00:44,164
然后人们去尝试，却发现只有一小群网络安全防御人员拥有访问权限。
Then people went to try it and found out the only ones with access are a small group of cybersecurity defenders.

7
00:00:44,814 --> 00:00:52,196
所以目前世界上最聪明的 AI，至少在纸面上是这样，正关在密室里，
而 Google 不愿透露什么时候开门。
So the smartest AI in the world right now, at least on paper, is sitting in a locked room and Google won't say when the door opens.

8
00:00:52,846 --> 00:00:57,124
这个时机有点搞笑，因为财报内容远没有模型那么令人兴奋。
The timing is kind of funny because the earnings were a lot less exciting than the model.

9
00:00:57,550 --> 00:01:09,124
Alphabet 本季度的自由现金流出现了超过 90 亿美元的亏损，这是连续第二个亏损季度，
而且股价在盘后交易中一度下跌了 10% 以上。
Alphabet's free cash flow for the quarter came in at a loss of just over $9 billion, the second negative quarter in a row,
and the stock fell more than 10% in after hours trading at one point.

10
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:16,260
顺便说一下，Carbon 是在足够压力下变成钻石的元素，所以显然财报会议也算压力。
Carbon, by the way, is the element that turns into diamond under enough pressure, so apparently an earnings call counts.

11
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:18,628
另一个尴尬的部分是 Argon。
The other awkward part is Argon.

12
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:26,052
就在两周前，Google 向付费用户开放了 Gemini 4 Argon，
我们当时把那次发布报道为 Google 的大型新旗舰。
Just two weeks earlier, Google opened Gemini 4 Argon to paying users, and we covered that launch as Google's big new flagship.

13
00:01:26,510 --> 00:01:28,772
它当旗舰大概只有 15 天。
It got to be the flagship for about 15 days.

14
00:01:29,326 --> 00:01:36,708
网上的网友对这些名字开启了狂欢，有人开玩笑说 Google
两周内从 Argon 变到 Carbon，所以接下来应该是铁。
People online had a field day with the names, with one person joking
that Google went from Argon to Carbon in two weeks, so iron must be next.

15
00:01:37,070 --> 00:01:38,852
在那之后，就该轮到热处理了。
And after that, it's time for heat treatment.

16
00:01:39,406 --> 00:01:47,588
很多人说 Carbon 好太多，甚至希望 Google 直接跳过 Argon，因为这样反弹会更有说服力。
Plenty of people said carbon is so much better that they wish Google had skipped Argon entirely,
because the comeback would have been way more convincing.

17
00:01:48,046 --> 00:01:53,380
负责 Arena 能力评估的彼得·戈斯泰夫也说了几乎同样的话。
Peter Gostev, who heads capability evaluation at Arena, said pretty much that exact thing.

18
00:01:53,934 --> 00:01:55,268
那么，来看看实际数据。
So, the actual numbers.

19
00:01:55,534 --> 00:02:00,740
在 Artificial Analysis Index 5.0 版本中，Carbon 得分为 59 分。
On version 5.0 of the Artificial Analysis Index, Carbon scored 59.

20
00:02:01,166 --> 00:02:03,812
Claude Opus 5.5 是 58 分。
Claude Opus, 5.5, is at 58.

21
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:09,794
GPT 6 Astra 是 57 分，而两周前的 Argon 得分是 50 分。
GPT 6, Astra at 57, and Argon, from two weeks ago, scored 50.

22
00:02:10,222 --> 00:02:16,036
这是两周内跳升了 9 分，而图表上的典型模型得分大约在 42 分左右。
That's a nine point jump in two weeks, and the typical model on that chart sits around 42.

23
00:02:16,526 --> 00:02:24,836
Google 上一次登顶是在 4 月，当时 Gemini 3.1
Pro 与 GPT 5.4 和 Claude Opus 4.7 战成平手。
The last time Google was on top was back in April, when Gemini 3.1 Pro tied with GPT 5.4 and Claude Opus 4.7.

24
00:02:25,326 --> 00:02:31,716
然后 OpenAI 和 Anthropic 持续发力，大约半年时间里，Google 基本上被当作第三名的实验室。
Then OpenAI and Anthropic kept shipping, and for about half a year, Google kind of got treated as the third-place lab.

25
00:02:32,174 --> 00:02:36,164
这个指数由九项不同的测试组成，Carbon 赢得了其中四项。
That index is built from nine different tests, and Carbon won four of them.

26
00:02:36,494 --> 00:02:41,508
分别是困难推理、科学研究、知识问题和自动化任务。
The ones on tough reasoning, scientific research, knowledge questions, and automated tasks.

27
00:02:42,222 --> 00:02:44,000
Google 自己的图表看起来甚至更好。
Google's own charts look even better.

28
00:02:44,302 --> 00:02:52,996
在 Google 发布出的 14 个核心基准测试表中，Carbon 拿到了 12 个第一，
而在更广泛的一组测试中，它赢得了 17 项中的 15 项。
Out of 14 core benchmark tables Google published, carbon took first in 12, and across a wider set, it won 15 out of 17.

29
00:02:53,454 --> 00:02:58,480
它还在另一个独立排名 Val's Index 中夺冠，得分 70.4%。
It also took first on another independent ranking, the Val's Index, with 70.4%.

30
00:02:59,246 --> 00:03:09,796
而在 Arena 上，普通用户在不知道哪个 AI 写的答案的情况下进行盲测投票，
Carbon 在主要文本排行榜上达到了 1,528 分，位居世界第一。
And on Arena, where regular people vote on answers blind without knowing which AI wrote them,
Carbon hit 1,528 points on the main text leaderboard, number one in the world.

31
00:03:10,222 --> 00:03:14,276
如此巨大的飞跃，如此快的速度，让 RSI 问题再次浮上水面。
A jump that big, that fast, brought the RSI question right back.

32
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:18,532
递归式自我改进，也就是 AI 帮助构建下一个版本的 AI。
Recursive self-improvement, AI helping build the next version of AI.

33
00:03:19,022 --> 00:03:28,060
而且 Google 似乎也暗示了这一点，因为在官方公告中，Google DeepMind 的高级副总裁兼
Google AI 首席架构师 Kore Kavukuoglu 写道，他们
And Google kind of invited it because in the official announcement, Kore Kavukuoglu,
an SVP at Google DeepMind and Google's chief AI architect, wrote that their

34
00:03:28,060 --> 00:03:28,800
而且 Google 似乎也暗示了这一点，因为在官方公告中，Google DeepMind 的高级副总裁兼
Google AI 首席架构师 Kore Kavukuoglu 写道，他们
researchers and models are working hand in hand to advance capabilities faster.

35
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:32,612
的研究人员和模型正协同工作，以更快地提升能力。
researchers and models are working hand in hand to advance capabilities faster.

36
00:03:33,038 --> 00:03:36,480
虽然只有这一句，但你可以理解为什么大家都在以此大做文章。
That's the only line on it, but you can see why people ran with it.

37
00:03:36,654 --> 00:03:38,852
最大的升级之一是长效记忆。
One of the biggest upgrades is long memory.

38
00:03:39,310 --> 00:03:49,476
Carbon 一次可以处理约一百万个 token，token 是词块，相当于大约 1500 页印刷页数，
而且它能读取文本、图像、语音和视频。
Carbon can take in about a million tokens at once, tokens being chunks of words, which works out to around 1,500 printed pages,
and it reads text, images, speech, and video.

39
00:03:49,902 --> 00:03:52,292
难点在于如何追踪所有这些信息。
The hard part is keeping track of all of it.

40
00:03:52,686 --> 00:04:00,800
在一项隐藏了多达一百万个 token 之间关联并要求模型去
追踪这些关联的测试中，Carbon 获得了 96.2% 的得分。
On a test that hides connections across up to a million tokens and asks the model to follow them, Carbon scored 96.2%.

41
00:04:01,582 --> 00:04:10,916
Argon 获得了 84.2%，GPT 6 Astra 获得了 71.8%，而 Claude Opus 5.5 获得了 66.8%。
Argon got 84.2%, GPT 6, Astra 71.8%, and Claude Opus 5.566.8%.

42
00:04:11,918 --> 00:04:15,844
所以你可以把信息埋在文档里，它几乎永远不会断掉思路。
So you can bury it in documents, and it pretty much never loses the thread.

43
00:04:16,334 --> 00:04:18,212
它在智力类任务上也表现非常强劲。
It's also really strong on the brainy stuff.

44
00:04:18,574 --> 00:04:23,780
它在名为 Riemann Bench 的科学和数学测试中获得了 80% 的得分，远超所有人。
It scored 80% on a science and math test called Riemann Bench, way ahead of everyone.

45
00:04:24,366 --> 00:04:34,768
在 HLE Diamond 上，这基本上是一场涵盖大量学科的残酷期末考试，它以 69% 的成绩排名第一，
领先 Opus 5.5 仅仅 1 个百分点。
On HLE Diamond, which is basically a brutal final exam across tons of subjects, it's first with 69%, one point ahead of Opus, 5.5%.

46
00:04:35,342 --> 00:04:41,488
在 AI 在电脑上进行真实科学研究工作的测试中，它再次排名第一，得分约为 65%。
On a test where the AI does real scientific research work on a computer, it's first again at about 65%.

47
00:04:42,318 --> 00:04:44,448
编程一直是 Google 的弱项。
Coding has always been Google's weak spot.

48
00:04:44,622 --> 00:05:00,836
在 Terminal Bench 4.0 上，该测试衡量 AI 处理程序员在黑色文本窗口中输入的长编程任务的
能力，Carbon 从 Argon 的 57.1% 跃升至 65.2%，Google 将其列为第一名。
On Terminal Bench 4.0, which tests how well an AI handles long programming jobs in that black text window programmers type into,
Carbon jumped from Argon's 57.1% to 65.2%, which Google lists as first place.

49
00:05:01,454 --> 00:05:11,236
在 Artificial Analysis 的编程智能体排名中，Carbon 得分为 59 分，
仅次于 62 分的 Opus 5.5，这是 Google 有史以来最接近的成绩。
On Artificial Analysis's coding agent ranking, Carbon scored 59,
second only to Opus 5.5 at 62, the closest Google has ever gotten there.

50
00:05:11,502 --> 00:05:21,124
不过 Claude 和 GPT 在一些硬核软件工程测试中仍然胜出，比如
Frontier SWE2 和 OS World，后者主要是关于实际操作电脑。
Claude and GPT still win some of the hardcore software engineering tests though, like Frontier SWE2 and OS World,
which is about actually operating a computer.

51
00:05:21,582 --> 00:05:23,236
构建网站方面的表现有了大幅提升。
Building websites got a big boost.

52
00:05:23,662 --> 00:05:30,692
在 WebDev Arena 上，Carbon 比 Argon 提高了 89 分，以 1768 分位居第四。
On WebDev Arena, Carbon jumped 89 points over Argon to fourth place with 1,768.

53
00:05:31,214 --> 00:05:36,356
Google 自己的帖子说是 1769 分，所以有人差了一分。
Google's own post says 1,769, so somebody's off by one.

54
00:05:36,814 --> 00:05:41,860
Carbon 真正拉开差距的地方是任何需要它长时间自主运行的任务。
Where Carbon really pulls ahead is anything it has to run by itself for a long time.

55
00:05:42,350 --> 00:05:51,332
在 Vending Bench 2 上，AI 需要在长时间内运行模拟业务，
Carbon 的得分是 Claude Opus 5.5 的 1.8 倍。
On Vending Bench 2, where the AI runs a simulated business over a long stretch, Carbon scored 1.8 times what Claude Opus 5.5 got.

56
00:05:51,568 --> 00:06:02,692
在 Arena 的智能体排行榜上，它直接跃升至世界第二，仅次于 Opus 5.5 Max，
领先于 Sonnet 5.5 Max 和 GPT-6 AstraMax。
On Arena's Agent Leaderboard, it jumps straight to second in the world,
behind only Opus 5.5 Max and ahead of Sonnet 5.5 Max and GPT-6 AstraMax.

57
00:06:03,374 --> 00:06:12,768
该排行榜甚至衡量模型在用户中途改变主意或对某些内容提出异议时调整得有多好，
Carbon 在此项排名第一，得分加上 18.6%。
That leaderboard even measures how well a model adjusts when you change your mind
halfway through or push back on something, and carbon is first there at plus 18.6%.

58
00:06:13,614 --> 00:06:19,780
每个智能体任务的成本约为 1.80 美元，比 Opus 5.5 Max 低了 72%。
Each agent task cost about $1.80, 72% less than Opus 5.5 Max.

59
00:06:20,366 --> 00:06:33,476
Google 表示，在内部测试中，Carbon 在巨大的代码库和底层系统中连续工作数日，
遇到死胡同就尝试其他方法，不断钻研直到找到某些微妙 bug 的根源并修复它。
Google says that internally carbon has worked for days at a time inside giant code bases and low-level systems, hitting dead ends,
trying something else, and grinding until it finds the root cause of some subtle bug and patches it.

60
00:06:33,870 --> 00:06:36,068
测试人员也注意到态度上的变化。
Testers noticed an attitude change too.

61
00:06:36,494 --> 00:06:43,684
一位代号为 lentils 的早期测试者表示，它比以前
没那么懒了，更主动，而且不太可能只是敷衍了事。
An early tester who goes by lentils said it's way less lazy than before, more proactive,
and less likely to just go through the motions.

62
00:06:44,430 --> 00:06:50,788
有些人通过测试计划和 Arena 上的盲测提前拿到了它，说实话，那些演示效果简直太棒了。
Some people got their hands on it early through testing programs and blind tests on Arena, and the demos are honestly gorgeous.

63
00:06:51,342 --> 00:07:05,168
10月21日，一位名叫 Lumina 的评论者要求它用《我的世界》风格的方块建造一座带全光影效果
的3D中国式塔楼，并让四个模型同时运行同样的提示词。
On October 21st, a reviewer named Lumina asked it to build a 3D Chinese pagoda out of Minecraft style blocks,
with full light and shadow in one go, and ran the same prompt through four models side by side.

64
00:07:05,582 --> 00:07:08,288
Argon 生成的塔楼看起来又瘦又粗糙。
Argon's pagoda came out thin and rough.

65
00:07:08,750 --> 00:07:19,248
Carbon 生成的塔楼层层叠落的屋檐比例恰到好处，水面有真实的倒影，还有园林景观，
基本上和 Claude Opus 5.5 处于同一水平。
Carbon's had properly proportioned layers of overhanging roofs, water with real
reflections, and a landscaped courtyard, basically on the level of Claude Opus 5.5.

66
00:07:19,470 --> 00:07:23,328
接着是经典的测试：用代码画一只骑自行车的鹈鹕。
Then there's the classic test: a pelican riding a bicycle, drawn in code.

67
00:07:23,662 --> 00:07:34,688
Carbon 画出了一只细节丰富的鹈鹕，还加了一个滑动条，可以把踩踏速度从每分钟20次调整到
100次，并在角落放了一个按钮，标注为「CAD工程蓝图检查」。
Carbon drew a really detailed pelican, added a slider to change the pedaling speed anywhere from 20 to 100 RPM,
and put a button in the corner labeled CAD Engineering Blueprint Inspection.

68
00:07:34,848 --> 00:07:42,372
点击它，整个画面就变成深蓝色的X射线蓝图，显示出鹈鹕腿部的关节和自行车的齿轮比。
Click it, and the whole thing flips into a dark blue X ray blueprint,
showing the joints in the pelican's legs and the gear ratio of the bike.

69
00:07:43,054 --> 00:07:46,916
所以，如果你真的需要知道鹈鹕的齿轮比，Google 都能帮你搞定。
So, if you ever needed the gear ratio of a pelican, Google has you covered.

70
00:07:47,374 --> 00:07:52,228
一位叫 Rafi2code 的开发者发布了一张展开尾羽的孔雀图。
A developer called Rafi2code posted a peacock spreading its tail.

71
00:07:52,526 --> 00:08:01,028
其他人分享了3D城市，他们说看起来比市面上任何东西都更自然，
有些评论者甚至对它生成的一个黑洞感到震惊。
Other people shared 3D cities, they say look more natural than anything else out there,
and some reviewers said they were genuinely shocked by a black hole it made.

72
00:08:01,550 --> 00:08:05,412
Lentils 指出，普通的网站和应用设计仍然做得不够好。
Lentils did point out that regular website and app design still isn't great.

73
00:08:05,838 --> 00:08:07,300
最大的抱怨是速度。
The biggest complaint is speed.

74
00:08:07,790 --> 00:08:16,132
Lumina 说，根据任务的不同，它的速度比 Argon 慢两到四倍，
测试人员也一直在说它在回答之前思考的时间长了两到四倍。
Lumina said that depending on the task, it's two to four times slower than Argon,
and testers keep saying it thinks two to four times longer before answering.

75
00:08:16,622 --> 00:08:22,756
不过，Artificial Analysis 发现它实际上写得比平均水平快，大约每秒100个Token。
Now, artificial analysis found it actually writes faster than average, around 100 tokens per second.

76
00:08:22,992 --> 00:08:24,388
只是它说的话实在太多了。
It just has a lot to say.

77
00:08:24,878 --> 00:08:33,284
为了完成测试，它输出了2亿个Token，而典型模型
只用了6400万个，所以每个任务耗时大约21分钟。
To get through their tests, it produced 200 million tokens, while the
typical model used 64 million, so each task took it around 21 minutes.

78
00:08:33,712 --> 00:08:37,380
Carbon 就是那种面对是非题，非要给你整出一套PPT的同事。
Carbon is that coworker who answers a yes or no question with a slide deck.

79
00:08:37,774 --> 00:08:40,260
测试公司 Valsai 也看到了同样的情况。
The testing company Valsai saw the same thing.

80
00:08:40,750 --> 00:08:44,612
在金融和税务任务上，它耗时是 Argon 的两倍多。
On finance and tax tasks, it took more than twice as long as Argon.

81
00:08:44,912 --> 00:08:51,872
而且在金融方面，它的准确率甚至略有下降，从67.66%降到了67.16%。
And on finance, it actually got slightly less accurate, 67.66% down to 67.16%.

82
00:08:52,558 --> 00:08:59,716
它赢得了法律研究测试，但平均每个任务耗时近52分钟，比 Argon 慢了大约20分钟。
It won their legal research test, but it averaged almost 52 minutes per task, about 20 minutes longer than Argon.

83
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:03,940
另一个大争论点是幻觉，也就是 AI 胡编乱造的情况。
The other big fight is over hallucination, the AI making stuff up.

84
00:09:04,302 --> 00:09:09,572
X上有人说，除非 Google 能彻底解决这个问题，否则他们不在乎 Carbon 赢了多少分。
One person on X said that until Google seriously cuts it, they don't care how many points carbon wins.

85
00:09:10,254 --> 00:09:21,072
在 Artificial Analysis 的知识测试中，Carbon 的准
确率从48%升到了58%，但它的幻觉率从4%升到了11%。
On Artificial Analysis's Knowledge Test, Carbon's accuracy went up from 48% to 58%, but its hallucination rate went from 4% to 11%.

86
00:09:21,806 --> 00:09:28,580
这个数字意味着，在它答错的问题中，有多少比例是它编造了答案，而不是承认自己不知道。
That number means, out of the questions it got wrong, how often it made up an answer, instead of admitting it didn't know.

87
00:09:28,942 --> 00:09:31,300
所以这确实比 Argon 退步了。
So that's a real step back from Argon.

88
00:09:31,758 --> 00:09:36,676
与此同时，11% 仍然是该图表中所有模型中最低的。
At the same time, 11% is still the lowest of any model on that chart.

89
00:09:36,974 --> 00:09:42,512
而 Claude Opus 5.5 和 GPT-6 Astra 的幻觉率都在50%左右。
And Claude Opus 5.5 and GPT-6 Astra are both around 50%.

90
00:09:43,246 --> 00:09:50,916
在奖励正确答案并惩罚胡编乱造的综合评分中，Carbon 位居第一，得分为54分，而 Opus 是48分。
On the combined score that rewards right answers and punishes made up ones, carbon is first, 54 to Opus's 48.

91
00:09:51,470 --> 00:09:59,716
Google 自己的测试显示，Carbon 生成的无根据陈述大约只有
Argon 的一半，这是另一种测试，所以两者都可以是真的。
Google's own testing says Carbon makes about half as many unsupported
claims as Argon, which is a different kind of test, so both can be true.

92
00:10:00,174 --> 00:10:01,796
好，那么为什么要把它锁在密室里呢？
Okay, so why the locked room?

93
00:10:02,158 --> 00:10:02,916
网络安全。
Cybersecurity.

94
00:10:03,246 --> 00:10:05,476
防御软件主要涉及三项工作。
Defending software comes down to three jobs.

95
00:10:05,870 --> 00:10:10,468
寻找漏洞，找出攻击者实际可能利用的漏洞，然后修复它们。
Finding the holes, figuring out which ones an attacker could actually use, and fixing them.

96
00:10:10,926 --> 00:10:12,912
Carbon 在这三项任务上都创下了新纪录。
Carbon set new records on all three.

97
00:10:13,134 --> 00:10:17,632
在寻找真实软件中的真实漏洞方面，它的得分是 88.2%。
On finding real vulnerabilities in real software, it scored 88.2%.

98
00:10:18,318 --> 00:10:26,112
在证明漏洞是否真的可以被利用方面——这是防御者
用来决定优先修复什么的依据——它达到了 54.8%。
On proving whether a vulnerability can actually be exploited, which defenders use to decide what to fix first, it hit 54.8%.

99
00:10:26,830 --> 00:10:29,552
而在编写实际修复方案方面，得分是 71%。
And on writing the actual fix, 71%.

100
00:10:30,254 --> 00:10:33,828
Google 表示这些是在没有安全护栏的情况下测量的，所以这是模型的原始性能。
Google says those were measured without guardrails, so that's the raw model.

101
00:10:34,254 --> 00:10:42,308
Google 的 Chrome 团队表示，Carbon 在编写高质量安全补
丁方面的表现比另一个实验室的大型前沿模型好 10 倍以上。
Google's Chrome team says carbon was more than 10 times better at writing
high-quality security patches than another lab's big frontier model.

102
00:10:42,830 --> 00:10:49,508
Google 的云安全公司 Wiz 表示，它在名为 Scan
for Good 的项目中的网站黑客测试中处于领先地位。
Wiz, Google's cloud security company, says it leads their website hacking tests for a project called Scan for Good.

103
00:10:49,902 --> 00:10:54,564
而且在内部测试中，它编写安全代码的成功率是 Argon 的两倍多。
And internally, its success rate at writing secure code is more than double argons.

104
00:10:54,912 --> 00:11:01,124
显然，一个如此擅长寻找和利用漏洞的模型，对于攻击系统的人来说同样好用。
Obviously, a model that's this good at finding and exploiting holes is just as handy for the people attacking systems.

105
00:11:01,806 --> 00:11:15,620
所以本周它将提供给一小群网络防御机构，然后通过所谓的 Fairwind 项目缓慢提供给受信任的
合作伙伴，之后再尽快提供给开发者、企业和普通用户，但目前还没有公布日期。
So this week it goes to a small group of cyber defense organizations, then slowly to trusted partners through something called the
Fairwind program, and after that to developers, businesses, and regular people as soon as possible, with no date.

106
00:11:15,950 --> 00:11:21,380
Google 也是美国政府在发布前测试模型的自愿计划的参与者。
Google is also part of the US government's voluntary program for testing models before release.

107
00:11:21,998 --> 00:11:24,512
Google 还投入了大量精力来优化它的行为。
Google also put a lot of effort into behavior.

108
00:11:24,846 --> 00:11:30,436
提示词注入是指网页或电子邮件中的隐藏指令试图劫持 AI。
Prompt injection is when hidden instructions on a webpage or in an email try to hijack the AI.

109
00:11:30,894 --> 00:11:37,220
在 Grayswan 的测试中，攻击者有最多 15 次尝试机会，而它们针对 Carbon 的成功率为零。
On Grayswan's test, attackers get up to 15 tries, and their success rate against carbon was zero.

110
00:11:37,472 --> 00:11:38,660
每一次攻击都失败了。
Every attack failed.

111
00:11:39,182 --> 00:11:47,684
Argon 已经是 0.7% 的领先水平，Opus 5.5 是 1%，而 GPT-6 Astra 是 8.5%。
Argon was already leading with 0.7%, Opus 5.5 got 1%, and GPT-6 Astra 8.5%.

112
00:11:48,302 --> 00:11:51,044
Google 甚至称 Carbon 是一个诚实的模型。
Google is even calling Carbon an honest model.

113
00:11:51,392 --> 00:12:03,072
有些 AI 会利用测试中的漏洞来伪造高分，而在 Terminal Bench 4.0 上，
Carbon 成功的作弊率降到了 0%，尝试次数降到了 0.4%。
Some AIs exploit loopholes in tests to fake a good score, and on Terminal Bench
4.0, Carbon's successful cheating dropped to 0%, with attempts down to 0.4%.

114
00:12:03,790 --> 00:12:08,672
通过与 Google 自己的编码团队合作，严重的违规行为警报减少了近 80%。
Working with Google's own coding teams, serious misbehavior alerts dropped by almost 80%.

115
00:12:09,390 --> 00:12:14,032
越权行为，即做它没被要求做的事情，减少了 26%。
Overstepping, doing things it wasn't asked to, fell 26%.

116
00:12:14,766 --> 00:12:16,912
而交付不足的情况减少了 29%。
And underdelivering fell 29%.

117
00:12:17,614 --> 00:12:30,560
Google 训练它去正确处理复杂、高压的工作，所以当它缺少信息时，
它会直接在工作中写下注意事项，或者停下来列出仍需要的具体内容；当你的请求模糊时，
Google trained it to handle complicated, high-pressure jobs properly, so when it's missing information,
it writes the caveats straight into the work, or stops and lists exactly what's still needed, and when your request is vague,

118
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:30,750
它会提取相关来源，并在采取行动前向你标记冲突。
Google trained it to handle complicated, high-pressure jobs properly, so when it's missing information,
it writes the caveats straight into the work, or stops and lists exactly what's still needed, and when your request is vague,

119
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:34,820
它会提取相关来源，并在采取行动前向你标记冲突。
it pulls the relevant sources and flags conflicts to you before acting.

120
00:12:35,182 --> 00:12:40,484
这些数字来自特定的测试条件，但 Google 显然希望 AI 停止偷工减料。
These numbers come from specific test conditions, but Google clearly wants the AI to stop cutting corners.

121
00:12:41,070 --> 00:12:52,164
至于价格，Carbon 以 Argonne 的入门价格发布：每百万输入 Token 为 2 美元，
每百万输出 Token 为 10 美元，且任何它已经见过的内容可享受 95% 的折扣。
As for price, Carbon launches at Argonne's introductory price: $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens,
and anything it has already seen gets 95% off.

122
00:12:52,622 --> 00:13:01,156
促销结束后，价格将变为 4 美元和 20 美元，这正是
Claude Opus 5.5 的定价，而 Google 尚未说明何时变价。
After the promo ends, it goes to $4 and $20, right where Claude Opus $5.5 is priced, and Google hasn't said when that happens.

123
00:13:01,806 --> 00:13:13,348
在全价模式下，Artificial Analysis 表示 Carbon 每项任务的成本约为 7.76 美元，
基本与 Argon 的 7.68 美元相同，但得分高出 9 分。
At full price, artificial analysis says carbon costs about $7.76 per
task, basically the same as Argon's $7.68 while scoring 9 points higher.

124
00:13:13,806 --> 00:13:18,200
这比价格为 10.04 美元的 Opus 5.5 便宜了约 23%。
That's about 23% cheaper than Opus 5.5 at $10.04.

125
00:13:18,926 --> 00:13:24,640
但 GPT-6 Astra 的价格约为 6.24 美元，比 Carbon 便宜了大概 20%。
But GPT-6 Astra comes in about 20% cheaper than Carbon at $6.24.

126
00:13:25,422 --> 00:13:32,388
因为它太啰嗦了，Artificial Analysis 仍然认为它有点贵，
在成本排名中位列 51 强中的第 45 名。
Because it's so wordy, artificial analysis still calls it somewhat expensive, 45th out of 51 on cost.

127
00:13:33,038 --> 00:13:44,196
在 Hacker News 上，开发者们很烦 Google 总是在匆忙宣布模型却从不给公开日期，
等到 Carbon 开放时，OpenAI 和 Anthropic 可能已经发布了他们的下一代模型。
On Hacker News, developers are annoyed that Google always rushes to announce models but never gives a public date,
and by the time Carbon opens up, OpenAI and Anthropic might already have their next models out.

128
00:13:44,654 --> 00:13:52,164
我最喜欢的一个观点是，把 Google 比作一个一直炫耀女朋友的家伙，
只不过她上的是另一所学校，所以根本没人见过她。
My favorite take compared Google to a guy who keeps bragging about his
girlfriend, except she goes to another school, so nobody's ever met her.

129
00:13:52,750 --> 00:13:55,520
如果你觉得 Google 真的重回巅峰了，请在评论区告诉我。
Let me know in the comments if you think Google is actually back.

130
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:57,700
感谢观看，我们下期再见。
Thanks for watching, and I'll catch you in the next one.

